# Alinea / Rhys Elliot milestones are keepers

**Alinea Analytics** and **Rhys Elliot** (analyst at Alinea) are the same high-value source family. Figures attributed to either — including press echoes that only name Rhys Elliot — are **precise and precious** for the model. Treat them as keepers, not junk third-party noise.

## Do

- Keep Alinea- and Rhys-Elliot-attributed milestones visible (`rejectedAt` null).
- Prefer them over vague MEDIA echos of the same claim when deduping or resolving same-day conflicts.
- When cleaning “estimates”, exclude **both** Alinea and Rhys Elliot from soft-reject / deactivate lists.
- Preserve when host or attribution matches any of:
  - hosts: `alineaanalytics.com`, `alineaanalytics.substack.com`
  - names: `Alinea`, `Alinea Analytics`, `Rhys Elliot`, `Rhys Elliott` (spelling variants)

## Do not

- Soft-reject or hard-delete because the note/publisher cites Alinea **or** Rhys Elliot alone.
- Treat “Rhys Elliot” as a generic industry analyst to junk (he is Alinea).
- Lump this family with SteamSpy / SteamDB / Sensor Tower / VG Insights / “third-party statistics”.
- Blacklist Alinea hosts or block them in discovery/ingest.
- Assume `isEstimate=true` means “discard” for this family — they remain useful for the algo.

## Contrast (OK to treat as low-trust estimates)

SteamSpy, SteamDB owners, Sensor Tower, VG Insights, generic “third-party statistics” without Alinea/Rhys Elliot — these may be flagged or soft-rejected when clearly non-declared.
